  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_006, RNA-only/multi-profile/scVI_n200/transformer, acc=0.653) shows that multi-profile scVI_n200 is the dominant configuration, and transformer vs avgpool aggregation makes negligible difference. The only untested RNA encoder is scGPT. Question: Does scGPT outperform scVI_n200 as the RNA encoder in the multi-profile + transformer setting? This is a clean single-variable change from config_006. Why this is the best next experiment: With 4 experiments remaining, establishing whether scGPT offers a stronger RNA representation before committing budget to multimodal fusion is critical. If scGPT is superior, it becomes the foundation for the strongest multimodal configs; if not, we confirm scVI_n200 as the best encoder and can dedicate remaining budget to testing whether multimodal fusion adds value on top of the proven RNA-only best."
}

